**New evidence**
- 2022 election-law process was contested; the opposition boycotted the National Assembly debate because it wanted the CENI composition reviewed.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC: débat général ce vendredi à l'Assemblée nationale sur la réforme de la loi électorale","publisher":"Actualite.cd","publication_date":"2022-04-22","url":"https://actualite.cd/2022/04/22/rdc-debat-general-ce-vendredi-lassemblee-nationale-sur-la-reforme-de-la-loi-electorale","claim":"The opposition boycotted the Assembly debate on electoral-law reform because it wanted first a consensus on reviewing CENI composition.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Congolese reporting on a concrete parliamentary process with named institutions and parties.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target year 2022; directly about the election-law environment Tshisekedi governed.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Tshisekedi's governing coalition and the institutional setup it oversaw, though the article reports opposition behavior rather than a presidential order.","contrary_evidence":["Boycott itself does not prove unilateral manipulation, only that the process lacked broad trust."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.2","4B.4","4B.10"]}

